title Caravan bear -- a plan may name the loss it would rather carry than repair
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; condense REMEMBER when a set closes; send each finished increment
think Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE before anything else, then the operator card, then the top three rows of the log index and the newest recommend lines. The reds queue is clear -- REDS %96 and %97 both closed on the lap below -- so Standfast opens no gate and this lap is a rung rather than a repair.
think The mend rung's own recommend named the question standing above it: a repair that fails is a second loss, and a run that mends the same arc forever is a supervisor with no way to stop. Reading mend.rye whole, the sharper half of that question is the one it never asks -- the mend repairs every arc it lost, because nothing in the record ever told it otherwise.
think So the rung is the plan's own word about its losses. A phase written bear = true says: if this arc is lost, carry the loss. The measurement that follows is new in kind for this arc -- every count before it weighs a harm, and this weighs an overreach. The plan comes out complete under the elder reading either way, which is exactly why nothing below could see it.
think Built the module as this ladder builds them: the supervisor carried whole from the rung below, with one question added and every refusal beneath it still standing. Phase gains one field and a below() conversion; Report wraps mend's; the reckoning writes a bearing note beside the loss note; the repair seats what the bearing spares.
think The lap needed two absorbed-and-lost arcs to part the readings, and the first cut only lost one. Instrumented confer_slot rather than guessing: the head never reached the fourth phase, because client_a's stand contended with client_b on a board write and the fourth phase passed the blocked head as its own dependent. Letting client_a read the board rather than write it -- still inside the grant the document carries -- put the head where the conferral could happen.
think Six RED paths proven on metal before the claim. One landed as a bare invariant panic rather than a named refusal, so the run refusal moved ahead of the assert: a supervisor reaching past the wire it read is now stopped by name before it spawns anything, and the invariant beneath it never has to catch it in the act.
obs The finding is the first of this arc that weighs obedience rather than harm. An overclaim is a sentence a supervisor should not have written; unserved work is an arc nobody carried; this is work a run did that it was asked not to do -- and a plan repaired against its own word still reads as carried out, which is what made it invisible.
obs The settlement earning a third word is the honest half of the design. Reporting a plan short when its whole remaining loss is loss its author chose to carry would send an operator looking for work nobody wants done.
obs The council rota doc this lap was item 13, the happy zone and the thin edge. Its argument is the shape of this rung's own self-test: every question about the moment, the work, and the honesty of the count answered as a pure fold with no process anywhere, and only the answer -- what the wire published about the run's obedience -- left to the run itself.
loom witness=caravan_bear_witness phases=4 dependents_repairing=4 dependents_bearing=3 absorbed=2 lost=2 overrepaired_repairing=1 overrepaired_bearing=0 bore_bearing=1 unserved_bearing=1 reds_proven=6
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=57 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=true
file caravan/bear.rye the rung -- a plan's own word about which losses to carry, read from the wire before any repair seats a phase
file tools/caravan_bear_witness.rish the witness -- one plan run twice, obedience the only number that moves, both notes read off the wire an operator reads
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir gains its 57th rung, so the bijection holds and nothing lands unheard
file caravan/README.md the durable per-rung record, written where a reader of the module finds it
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to this rung, and the one below folds into the condensed pointer
recommend keep-going the arc has now answered for reach at every moment of a dependent's life, repaired what a fall cost, and learned which losses to leave alone -- so the question standing above it is the one the plan cannot answer alone: a bearing is a judgment made before the run, and some losses only reveal what they were worth after it, which asks whether a supervisor may ever weigh a loss its author left unmarked.
